### What was changed

Guards, markers, and the `#include` lines named above. **39 `// PIE:` markers
across 12 of the 24 files, 156 added lines**; the other 12 files are
byte-identical to upstream. Only **two** `#ifndef __CUDACC_RTC__` directives
remain in the whole FlashInfer tree, both in `attention/mla.cuh`, both
two-sided; there were thirty-three markers over ten files when every guard was
still a guard.
Every copyright header is intact and untouched. Nothing was reformatted,
renamed, reordered or "improved" -- include order in particular is upstream's,
which is why several files carry four small markers where one large one would
have needed a line moved.

A guard existed because NVRTC compiles for the device only. It refuses a
function marked `__host__` outright ("a function explicitly marked as a
__host__ function is not allowed in JIT mode"), it has no C++ standard
library, and it has no include path -- so `<iostream>`, `<sstream>`,
`<vector>`, the `cudaLaunchKernel` wrappers and the `std::ostringstream` error
paths had to be hidden from it. They are no longer hidden: they are gone, and
a marker records each one. The ahead-of-time build that used to see upstream
exactly by defining no `__CUDACC_RTC__` no longer exists -- there is no nvcc
in this crate -- so nothing was left to serve by keeping the text.

Each change is preceded by a marker of one of two fixed forms:

    // PIE: guarded for NVRTC -- <what and why>. Upstream is unmodified apart
    // from markers of this form; see NOTICE. Removing them restores the file.

    // PIE: REMOVED -- <what stood here>. <N> lines of host C++, <why removing
    // it changes no compile>. This marker is one a strip does NOT undo; see
    // MODIFICATIONS.

One `grep -rn "// PIE:" kernels/flashinfer/ --include='*.cuh'
--include='*.h'` finds all 39; 35 of the 39 are `REMOVED`, and 40 across both
trees are. The `--include` is load-bearing and was missing from this
sentence: the bare grep answers more than 39, because `MODIFICATIONS` sits in
that directory and quotes the marker form throughout its own prose -- and
answers more again after every edit to that page, which is why no number is
given for it here. The XQA grep below needs no such filter: that directory
holds sources and `LICENSE` and nothing else. The boilerplate sentence appears
once per file, on its first marker.
`kernels/flashinfer/MODIFICATIONS` lists the count per file, and the
property that list asserts -- *strip the markers, the `#ifndef` under each and
its matching `#endif`, and put back what a REMOVED marker names, and every
file is byte-for-byte upstream* -- was checked mechanically, per file, against
the CPM tree before this NOTICE was written.
`tests/upstream_manifest.rs` re-checked the half of that claim which needs no
network -- every file's guard count, added-line count, line count and byte
count against the table, and that the strip is still well defined for every
file -- and **it is deleted**, at `1a08b179a`, with the twelve other test
